ue] [17592186523202 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523202 1071 "In what direction does the function $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ decrease most rapidly at the point $(1,1)?$" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523202 1072 #uuid "48a5b0a5-ecb9-5e4e-bbb7-138d96fc81cd" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523202 1074 "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ decreases most rapidly in the direction opposite to that of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(1,1) & =(4\\cdot (1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))+4\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))\\text{ }i+(2(1)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1))\\text{ }j \\\\  & =8 \\sin{(1 )}\\text{ }i-2 \\cos{(1 )}\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function decreases most rapidly in the direction of $-8 \\sin{(1 )}\\,i+2 \\cos{(1 )}\\,j.$" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523203 1080 "-8 \\sin{(1 )}\\,i-6 \\cos{(1 )}\\,j" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523203 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523203 1083 #uuid "4a6a4fac-5734-5eb0-9ed6-a928757ce0a9" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523204 1080 "⟨\\frac{3 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17}⟩" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523204 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523204 1083 #uuid "4d2355f9-7bdf-5219-b0ed-8b759d10a82f" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523205 1080 "⟨-\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩" 1319413