39535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523210 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523210 1083 #uuid "65dd24b1-670c-595e-ac35-85b55310a28c" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523211 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523228 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523211 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523211 1071 "In what unit direction does the function $f(x,y,z)=\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4})$ increase most rapidly at the point $(1,1,1)$?" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523211 1072 #uuid "6d226b9a-26b3-5e84-bd16-a03937995368" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523211 1074 "At a given point, a function $f(x,y,z)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}))⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{1}{x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}}\\cdot 3x^{2}y^{2}z^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}}\\cdot 2x^{3}y^{1}z^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}}\\cdot 4x^{3}y^{2}z^{3}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{3}{x},\\,\\frac{2}{y},\\,\\frac{4}{z}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(1,1,1) & =⟨\\frac{3}{1},\\,\\frac{2}{1},\\,\\frac{4}{1}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding unit direction is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{∇f(1,1,1)}{‖∇f(1,1,1)‖} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(4)^{2}}}⟨3,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{3 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{4 \\sqrt{29}}{29}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the unit direction of $⟨\\frac{3 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{4 \\sqrt{29}}{29}⟩.$" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523212 1080 "⟨\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{2}{9}⟩" 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [17592186523212 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535618 17592186045443 true] [1759218652321